      "title": "Pewter Ingot",
      "category": "materials/1-common/metals/pewter-ingot",
      "source": "materials/1-common/metals/pewter-ingot/index.md",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Pewter Ingot\nslug: pewter-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot (Alloy)\nmaterial_family: Pewter\nsource_items:\n  - Tin Ingot\n  - Copper Ingot\n  - Lead Ingot\n  - Antimony Ingot\nweight: 1.0kg\nweight_class: Light\ndurability: Low\nenchantment_affinity: \"15% (+1 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 16 Marks\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Pewter Ingot\n\n## Effect\nPewter is a balanced, multi-metal alloy designed for utility, ritual use, and low-tier equipment. While not suited for heavy combat, it offers stability, adaptability, and strong interaction with minor enchantments.\n\n---\n\n## Crafting Use\n- Trinkets\n- Ritual tools\n- Containers\n- Light gear (limited)\n- Enchanted utility items\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Soft but structurally balanced  \n- Resistant to minor deformation due to antimony reinforcement  \n- Slightly toxic due to lead content  \n- Easy to shape and rework  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Composition\n- 2x [[Tin Ingot]] (Primary Base)\n- 1x [[Copper Ingot]]\n- 1x [[Lead Ingot]]\n- 1x [[Antimony Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Accepts low-tier enchantments easily  \n- Moderate stability for sustained effects  \n- Does not support high-tier enchantments  \n- Useful for:\n  - Wards\n  - Minor charms\n  - Ritual casting tools  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Notes\n- Limited use in weapons (low durability)  \n- Not suitable for armor beyond decorative/light use  \n- Best used for non-combat equipment  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires:\n  - 2x [[Tin Ingot]]\n  - 1x [[Copper Ingot]]\n  - 1x [[Lead Ingot]]\n  - 1x [[Antimony Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Not made for war, but for the quiet work that shapes it.\"*\n"
