      "source": "materials/2-uncommon/metals/platinum-ingot/index.md",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Platinum Ingot\nslug: platinum-ingot\ntype: item\nkingdom: Material\nitem_class: Uncommon\ncategory: Ingot\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ingot\nmaterial_family: Platinum\nsource_items:\n  - Platinum Ore\nweight: 1.1kg\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: High\nenchantment_affinity: \"40% (+3 dice)\"\ndamage_modifier: 1\narmor_modifier: 2\ntags:\n  - items\n  - materials\n  - metal\n  - ingot\n  - uncommon\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Platinum Ingot\n\n## Effect\nPlatinum is a rare and highly stable metal that excels in magical conductivity. It enhances divine and celestial enchantments while maintaining structural integrity.\n\n---\n\n## Crafting Use\n- Holy weapons\n- Relics\n- Enchanted armor\n- Magical cores\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Highly resistant to corruption  \n- Extremely stable under magical stress  \n- Difficult to forge without advanced methods  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- High-tier enchanted alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with Light and Celestial magic  \n- Increases enchantment effectiveness  \n- High stability under repeated casting  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +1 Damage Modifier\n- +2 Armor Modifier\n- Favours enchanted builds over raw damage  \n\n---\n\n## Crafting Source\n- Requires: 4x [[Platinum Ore]]\n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"Purity forged into form.\"*\n"
