      "category": "minerals/1-common/ores/iron-ore",
      "source": "minerals/1-common/ores/iron-ore/index.md",
      "content": "---\ntitle: Iron Ore\nslug: iron-ore\ntype: item\nkingdom: Mineral\nitem_class: Common\ncategory: Ore\nsubcategory: Metal\nmaterial_type: Metal\nmaterial_form: Ore\nmaterial_family: Iron\nsource_items: []\nrefines_into: Iron Ingot\nrefinement_ratio: \"4:1\"\nweight_class: Medium\ndurability: Moderate\nenchantment_affinity: \"10% (+0 dice)\"\nmarket_value: 3 Marks\nimage: Iron Ore.png\ntags:\n  - items\n  - minerals\n  - metal\n  - ore\n  - common\nvisibility: public\n---\n\n# Iron Ore\n\n## Effect\nIron Ore is dense and impurity-rich, requiring proper smelting to unlock its strength. Once refined, it forms the backbone of most weapons and armor.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nCalled the *“Blood of the World,”* iron runs deep beneath the earth. Civilizations rose and fell by their ability to mine and shape it.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Dense and widely available  \n- Requires stronger heat to refine  \n- Reliable base material for combat equipment  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Iron Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Requires stable heat for proper refinement\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Steel Ingot]]\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Neutral magical properties  \n- Supports basic rune and enchantment structures  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"From stone and fire, strength is born.\"*\n"
