      "content": "---\ntitle: \"Flowborn Undien\"\nslug: \"flowborn-undien\"\ntype: race\nraceCategory: \"Demi Races\"\nsecondaryCategory: \"Undien Races\"\ntertiaryCategory: \nplayable: true\nsize: \nmovement: \"9m\"\nlanguages:\n  - \"Common - Aquatic\"\nmagicAffinity:\n  - \"Water Magic\"\nessenceAffinity: []\ntags:\n  - \"race\"\n  - \"demi-races\"\n  - \"undien-races\"\nimages:\n  male: \"assets/races/flowborn-undien/flowborn-undien-male-adult.png\"\n  female: \"assets/races/flowborn-undien/flowborn-undien-female-adult.png\"\nvisibility: public\nsourceOrder: 180\n---\n\n# Flowborn Undien\n\n## Overview\n- Race Category: Demi-Race\n- Race Type: Spiritborn Humanoid\n- Parent Race: River Spirit × Humanoid\n- Playable: Yes\n- Rarity: Uncommon\n\n## Racial Features\n- Height Range:\n  - Male: 165cm - 190cm\n  - Female: 155cm - 180cm\n\n- Weight Range:\n  - 55kg - 95kg\n\n- Skin:\n  - Smooth and healthy appearance\n  - Warm to the touch\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Light Blue\n    - River Green\n    - Pale Teal\n    - Soft Silver\n    - Natural Human Tones with aquatic hues\n\n- Hair:\n  - Flows naturally even in still air\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Brown\n    - Black\n    - Blue\n    - Green\n    - Silver\n\n- Eyes:\n  - Bright and vibrant\n  - Colour Range:\n    - Emerald\n    - Teal\n    - Blue\n    - Silver\n    - Gold\n\n- Hands:\n  - Long graceful fingers\n  - Slight webbing\n\n- Face:\n  - Gentle and welcoming features\n  - Soft expressions\n\n- Ears:\n  - Slightly elongated\n  - Smooth fin-like ridges\n\n- Markings:\n  - Flowing river-like patterns\n  - Often glow softly when healing magic is used\n\n- Body:\n  - Lean and athletic\n  - Built for endurance and movement\n  - Naturally graceful posture\n\n---\n\n## Racial Characteristics\n| Characteristic | Buff/Debuff | Stat Rolls | Characteristics Tier Cap |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------ |\n| Strength       | -2          | 4d6        | Tier 3                   |\n| Dexterity      | +1          | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Agility        | +2          | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Constitution   | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Endurance      | +1          | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Intelligence   | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Wisdom         | 0           | 4d6        | Tier 5                   |\n| Charisma       | +1          | 4d6        | Tier 4                   |\n| Luck           | 0           | 3d6        | Tier 5                   |\n\n---\n\n## Racial Traits\n### Flow Sense\n\n#### Description\nFlowborn can instinctively feel the movement of water around them. Rivers, streams, rainfall, and currents act as extensions of their awareness.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Gain +2 Perception while within 30 metres of flowing water.\n- Can determine the direction of nearby water sources.\n- Gain advantage on Survival checks involving rivers, streams, and wetlands.\n- Cannot become naturally lost while following a waterway.\n\n---\n\n### Spirit of Renewal\n\n#### Description\nFlowborn embody the restorative nature of rivers and freshwater springs.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Healing effects received are increased by 10%.\n- Recover Stamina 25% faster during short rests.\n- Gain +1 to all healing magic rolls.\n- Natural healing is doubled while resting near fresh water.\n\n---\n\n### River Walker\n\n#### Description\nThe currents support the Flowborn wherever they travel.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Ignore movement penalties caused by shallow water, mud, marshes, and wetlands.\n- Gain advantage on Balance checks.\n- Swim speed equals double normal movement speed.\n- Can move across flowing water surfaces for up to 3 seconds before sinking.\n\n---\n\n### Breath of the Current\n\n#### Description\nFlowborn are equally comfortable above and below the water's surface.\n\n#### Gameplay Effect\n- Can breathe underwater indefinitely.\n- Ignore underwater combat penalties.\n- Gain resistance to exhaustion caused by swimming.\n- Never suffer penalties from strong river currents.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Culture\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Historical Figures\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Settlements\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Relations\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## Traits & Biology\n- Swim Speed: 18m\n- Ignore difficult terrain caused by rivers, marshes, wetlands, and shallow water.\n- Gain +3m movement speed while travelling alongside natural waterways.\n- Can swim continuously without fatigue for extended periods.\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Bonuses\n- Enhanced Healing\n- Excellent Endurance\n- Strong Survival Skills\n- Superior River Navigation\n- Natural Adaptability\n\n### ⚠️ Drawbacks\n- Less effective in deserts and arid climates.\n- Reduced comfort in saltwater environments.\n- Strong emotional connection to nature can make environmental destruction distressing.\n\n---\n\n## Gallery\nInformation coming soon.\n\n## GM Notes\nGM-only information coming soon.\n"
